  "id": "pincer-grip",
  "term": "pincer grip",
  "definition": "In this psychology context, pincer grip refers to a precision movement in which a person grips or releases an object using the thumb and index finger. It was used to study approach and avoidance behavior by treating gripping as approach and slipping as avoidance in response to positive or negative cues.",
